<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Wave L fixture: a SYNTHETIC Green Button feed carrying three itemized bills.

  Built by hand to reproduce the figures the 2026-10-07 data audit published
  as sums across three 29-day periods — $1,365.03 total, $311.61 delivery,
  $177.46 HST, -$320.78 rebate, $45.15 regulatory, $530.74/$218.71/$258.82
  off/mid/on — while keeping every per-period number self-consistent:

      Total = commodity + delivery + regulatory
      HST   = 13% of that subtotal, rounded per period
      rebate= 23.5% of it, rounded per period
      delivery ≈ $36.00 fixed + $0.0252/kWh (so the amortized split the panel
                shows is actually fitted, not asserted)

  It is NOT the app owner's Oakville Hydro export: no meter data, no account
  numbers, no read dates from a real bill (see tests/fixtures/README.md —
  the owner's own export must never enter this repo). The real file is used
  for the deployed browser check only; it is never committed.

  The LocalTimeParameters entry carries the same North-American DST rules
  every public fixture uses (360E2000 / B40E2000, tzOffset -18000).
-->
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:espi="http://naesb.org/espi" xml:lang="en-us">
    <id>urn:uuid:22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</id>
    <title>Synthetic Usage Summary feed (Wave L)</title>
